#!/usr/bin/env bash
# bin/onionwarden-fleet-diff — cross-fleet baseline diff report (PLAN §6 Phase 3).
#
# PLACEHOLDER — this is a Phase-3 deliverable and is out of scope for the
# current Phase 0-2 build. It is shipped as a stub so the CLI surface and the
# §3.3 layout are complete; the full implementation lands in Phase 3.
#
# When built, fleet-diff is an OPERATOR-SIDE tool (run from the receiver or an
# admin box, not a per-host check): it pulls each host's signed baseline
# manifest, normalises module/port/SUID/sshd/kernel posture, and emits a
# Markdown diff grouped by host and role so per-role anomalies stand out.
set -euo pipefail

cat >&2 <<'EOF'
onionwarden-fleet-diff: NOT YET IMPLEMENTED (Phase 3).

This is an operator-side cross-fleet baseline diff, scheduled for Phase 3 of
the rollout (PLAN §6). The current build covers Phases 0-2 only.

Phase-3 scope:
  - pull each host's signed baseline manifest from the receiver
  - normalise loaded modules / listening ports / SUID set / sshd posture /
    kernel + taint / installed-package set
  - emit a Markdown report grouped by host and role, surfacing the deltas
    WITHIN a role (one tor-relay carrying a module the other seven lack, etc.)

Until then, compare two single hosts with:
  onionwarden-baseline diff --baseline <dirA> --candidate <dirB>
EOF
exit 64
